# Canonicalise to www.robertopianastudio.it — the one host the sitemap and the
# rel=canonical tag both declare. Every alias 301s across (host-matched), the bare
# apex included, so nothing reads as duplicate content. These must stay above the
# path-only rules below, or the /* 404 would catch the aliases first.
#
# NOTE: the rpdesigngroup.com rule is currently INERT. That domain does not resolve
# to this Netlify site — a forwarding rule upstream (Hostinger) 301s every path to
# the root before Netlify ever sees it. Point its DNS here to make this line work.
https://robertopianastudio.it/*       https://www.robertopianastudio.it/:splat  301!
https://robertopianastudio.com/*      https://www.robertopianastudio.it/:splat  301!
https://www.robertopianastudio.com/*  https://www.robertopianastudio.it/:splat  301!
https://rpdesigngroup.com/*           https://www.robertopianastudio.it/:splat  301!

# The CMS lives only at /admin. Send the language-prefixed guess there.
# Forced (!) so it wins over the physical fallback page + the /en 404 below.
/en/admin/*  /admin/  301!
/en/admin    /admin/  301!

# Legacy rpdesigngroup.com paths. These still rank in Google (la-storia, contattaci,
# commerciale/showroom, chi-siamo/il-team) and the .com blanket-301s to this domain's ROOT,
# so the old deep links lose their target. Map each to its nearest surviving page instead of
# letting the /* rule below serve a 404 — that is what carries the ranking across.
/la-storia            /studio/    301
/chi-siamo/il-team    /studio/    301
/chi-siamo/*          /studio/    301
/contattaci           /contatti/  301
/commerciale/showroom /contatti/  301

# Language-aware 404. Existing files take precedence, so these only fire for
# unmatched paths. Specific rule first.
/en/*  /en/404.html  404
/*     /404.html      404
